  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<p>A research point is a feature representing single coordinate or point based locations, where some form of research observation, test, trial, measure, or monitoring activity has, or will take place. &nbsp;The mapped features are generally small in extent (for example, soil water table monitor, tree cavity nest), and can be used to represent the locations of sampling techniques (for example, basal area prism sweep).<br />This data class is one of three primitive data classes:</p><ul><li>Research Point (RESPOINT)</li><li>Research Line (RESLINE)</li><li>Research Polygon (RESPOLY) &nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Status:&nbsp;</strong><br />On going: data is continually being updated</p><p><strong>Maintenance and Update Frequency:</strong><br />As required&nbsp;</p><div><strong>Contact</strong><br />Calvin Julie, Natural Resources Information Unit</div><div><ul><li><a href='mailto:calvin.julie@ontario.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'>calvin.julie@ontario.ca</a>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Note</strong><br /><span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(74,74,74); font-family:inherit; font-size:16px;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:left; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>Additional features licensed under the Ontario Geospatial Data Exchange (OGDE) Agreement are available to members of the OGDE for professional, non-commercial use only. To find out more about the OGDE visit </span></span><a style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(0, 97, 155); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatu